    "title": "Bournemouth vs Manchester United Lineups, Injuries, Predictions, Live Streaming, How & Where to Watch on TV",
    "text": "The last Premier League weekend before the March international break will start with Bournemouth taking on Manchester United at Vitality Stadium.It is the 31st Premier League match for both teams this season, with Bournemouth currently 10th in the league table with 41 points and Manchester United 3rd with 54 points.AdvertisementAfter 30 league matches played, Bournemouth's record is nine wins, 14 draws, and seven losses. Manchester United's record is 15 wins, nine draws, and six losses.Bournemouth has four consecutive draws in the Premier League, and last weekend, Bournemouth drew 0-0 with Burnley away from home. Bournemouth have only scored one goal in their last four league games.Last weekend, Manchester United defeated Aston Villa 3-1 at Old Trafford with goals from Casemiro, Matheus Cunha, and Benjamin Sesko. Manchester United reached 3rd in the league table with that win over Aston Villa last weekend.AdvertisementManchester United hosted Bournemouth earlier this season on December 15, 2025, for the 16th matchweek. The match finished in a 4-4 draw at Old Trafford, with Eli Junior Kroupi scoring a late equalizer for Bournemouth.Eli Junior Kroupi of Bournemouth celebrates after he scores a goal to make it 4-4 during the Premier League match between Manchester United and Bournemouth at Old Trafford on December 15, 2025 in Manchester, England. (Photo by Robin Jones - AFC Bournemouth/AFC Bournemouth via Getty Images)Photo by Robin Jones - AFC Bournemouth/AFC Bournemouth via Getty Images (Photo by Robin Jones - AFC Bournemouth&sol;AFC Bournemouth via Getty Images)Official Lineups for Bournemouth and Manchester UnitedBournemouthGoalkeeper: Djordje PetrovicDefenders: Adrien Truffert, Marcos Senesi, James Hill, Alex JimenezMidfielders: Alex Scott, Ryan Christie, Marcus TavernierForwards: Rayan, Evanilson, Amine AdliInjuries: Julio Soler, Matal Akinmboni, Justin Kluivert, Lewis CookManchester UnitedGoalkeeper: Senne LammensDefenders: Luke Shaw, Harry Maguire, Leny Yoro, Diogo DalotMidfielders: Kobbie Mainoo, Casemiro, Bruno FernandesForwards: Matheus Cunha, Bryan Mbeumo, Amad DialloUnchanged XI to face Bournemouth 👊🤍— Manchester United (@ManUtd) March 20, 2026Injuries: Noussair Mazraoui, Lisandro Martinez, Matthijs De Ligt, Patrick DorguBournemouth vs Manchester United will kick off at 4 p.m. ET/ 1 p.m. PT in the United States. The match will kick off at 8 p.m. local time in Bournemouth, Dorset, England, at the Vitality Stadium.AdvertisementThe match will be available to watch across select TV channels and streaming services in the United States and the UK.USA Network (USA)TeleXitos (USA)NBC Universo (USA)USA 4K (USA)Sky Sports Main Event (UK)Sky Sports Premier League (UK)Sky Sports Ultra HDR (UK)Sky Go app, NOW TV (UK)Prediction: Bournemouth 1-2 Manchester UnitedThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 20, 2026, where it first appeared in the Soccer section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
